## Project Overview
AI coding assistant memory manager context. Working on a travel/tourism website with mobile menu, scroll reveal, and related frontend features across multiple JS and CSS files. Google Analytics tag added to both header files.

## Completed Work
- Reviewed project structure and architecture
- Identified areas for improvement
- Created implementation plan
- Read mobile menu section in `assets/js/inner.js` (lines 62–96)
- Modified `assets/js/inner.js` and `assets/js/main.js` mobile menu sections to add backdrop element creation and click-outside-to-close functionality
- Converted mobile menu to sidebar style in both CSS files and both JS files
- Added Google Analytics tag (G-S8DGBXB0JM) to both header files
- **Fixed backdrop click-blocking bug in both CSS files**: Changed from `display: none/block` toggling to `opacity + pointer-events` approach with CSS transition for smooth fade
- **Footer logo replaced in both footer files**: `<img src="/assets/image/logo.webp">` (height: 48px) replacing text-only logo spans
- **Fixed `destinations/china` footer issue**: Root cause was `china.php` using `overview` key (so `$isNewFormat = true`) but its `itineraries` use plain strings. Fix: Changed itinerary day rendering from format-based (`$isNewFormat`) to type-based (`is_array($day)`).
- **Fixed `.related-card-tag` color**: Changed from `var(--gold)` to hardcoded `#C9A84C` in `assets/css/inner.css`
- **Fixed all overlay text colors in `assets/css/inner.css`**: All card overlay text now uses hardcoded white/gold values instead of CSS variables (which are overridden to dark values in light theme)
- **Fixed china page cutoff after "Things to Do" tabs**: `country.php` line 191 was doing `$item['title']` and `$item['desc']` on plain strings in `experiences` arrays. Fix: Added `is_array($item)` check in the experiences tab panel loop. Now handles both array format and plain string format.
- **Current task**: Fix "Similar Destinations" section hover text readability issue in `assets/css/inner.css`

## Key Technical Decisions
- Mobile menu uses `open` class toggling on both `mobileMenu` and `hamburger` elements
- Body overflow set to `hidden` when menu is open
- Backdrop is a dynamically created `div.mobile-menu-backdrop` appended to `document.body`
- Backdrop gets `open` class toggled in sync with the menu
- Backdrop click triggers `closeMenu()`
- Mobile menu is sidebar style: slides in from right, `transform: translateX(100%)` → `translateX(0)`, `z-index: 99999`
- Backdrop: `position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 99998`
- **Backdrop fix**: Use `opacity: 0; pointer-events: none` (hidden) → `opacity: 1; pointer-events: all` (open) with `transition: opacity 0.35s ease` — applied to BOTH CSS files
- Google Analytics tag ID: `G-S8DGBXB0JM` — added to both header files
- Footer logo: absolute path `/assets/image/logo.webp` at height 48px
- `api/destination-single.php` uses `chdir(dirname(__DIR__))` to set working dir to project root, then `require 'destinations/country.php'`
- `country.php` supports two data formats: `$isNewFormat` (bool)
- **Itinerary fix**: Itinerary day rendering now uses `is_array($day)` check instead of `$isNewFormat`
- **Experiences fix**: Experience item rendering now uses `is_array($item)` check — handles both `['title'=>'...','desc'=>'...']` and plain string formats
- **CSS variable override issue**: `inner.css` redefines `--white: #1A1410` (dark brown) and `--gold: #B8860B` (dark gold) for light theme — all overlay text on dark image gradients must use hardcoded values

## Relevant Files & Code
### `assets/js/main.js` — `initMobileMenu()` (updated)
```js
function initMobileMenu() {
    const hamburger = document.getElementById('hamburger');
    const mobileMenu = document.getElementById('mobileMenu');
    const closeBtn  = document.getElementById('mobileMenuClose');
    if (!hamburger || !mobileMenu) return;

    let backdrop = document.querySelector('.mobile-menu-backdrop');
    if (!backdrop) {
        backdrop = document.createElement('div');
        backdrop.className = 'mobile-menu-backdrop';
        document.body.appendChild(backdrop);
    }

    function closeMenu() {
        mobileMenu.classList.remove('open');
        hamburger.classList.remove('open');
        backdrop.classList.remove('open');
        document.body.style.overflow = '';
    }

    hamburger.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const isOpen = mobileMenu.classList.toggle('open');
        hamburger.classList.toggle('open', isOpen);
        backdrop.classList.toggle('open', isOpen);
        document.body.style.overflow = isOpen ? 'hidden' : '';
    });

    if (closeBtn) closeBtn.addEventListener('click', closeMenu);
    mobileMenu.querySelectorAll('a').forEach(link => { link.addEventListener('click', closeMenu); });
    backdrop.addEventListener('click', closeMenu);
}
```

### Backdrop CSS — Both CSS files (fixed, same pattern)
```css
.mobile-menu-backdrop {
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.45);
  z-index: 99998;
  opacity: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  transition: opacity 0.35s ease;
}
.mobile-menu-backdrop.open {
  opacity: 1;
  pointer-events: all;
}
```

